---
description: Tech stack
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

- Python 3.10+ as the main development language.
- PyTorch for deep learning model development (bi-encoder, cross-encoder, training loops, mixed precision).
- Hugging Face Transformers for loading and fine-tuning pretrained encoder models (DeBERTa, RoBERTa, MiniLM, BGE).
- Sentence-Transformers for embedding model scaffolding, metric-learning losses (TripletLoss, CosineSimilarityLoss, MultipleNegativesRankingLoss), and training utilities.
- Datasets (HuggingFace Datasets) for easy JSONL loading, preprocessing, and splitting into folds.
- scikit-learn for k-fold cross-validation, metrics, and data preprocessing utilities.
- NumPy / Pandas for dataset manipulation, embeddings handling, and saving Track B .npy outputs.
- CUDA / RTX 4050 GPU with PyTorch GPU acceleration for all training tasks.
- PyYAML or JSON for configuration files defining model paths, hyperparameters, and reproducible experiment settings.
- tqdm for progress visualization during training and evaluation.
- zip / Unix CLI tools for preparing the final CodaBench submission.